      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOLDEN SUNSET (6) has returned in fine order, winning her two starts here off a spell. Raced in the death seat but toughed it out by 1.8m last time. Kept fresh since and draws wide but finds another suitable assignment so can land the hat trick. KEAYANG STUKA (3) has the hoof on the till having placed in all three appearances since switching to Queensland for this prep. The last two starts have been from 30m handicaps and he came from wider than this when resuming. Likely to get the favours from this nice draw. Big chance to break through. PINNIE (9) raced parked but stuck on for second to topliner Gus last week. That continued her good form that includes two recent wins here. Draws on the back row but is suited back to this distance having won three of the four times she has contested it here. MUFASA METRO NZ (7) owns a solid fresh record so is worth keeping safe along with ALDEBARANSTILINSKI (5) who also resumes but made decent progress last time in.",
